{
  "id": "ss.relic.burst",
  "name": "Burst sac",
  "description": "A sac at the moment it goes: a bright core — gold-white at the middle falling to ember at the edge — with three curled scraps of dark red wall still clinging round it, and nine spokes of hot ember thrown outward at uneven angles and lengths, with five loose specks beyond their tips. The overkill of a kill is what bursts into the bodies around it, so the picture is the leftover energy leaving the body, and it leaves in every direction at once but not tidily; the spokes are irregular so it is a splat and not a badge. The centre is the brightest part and is kept that way on purpose — a dark middle inside a ring of spikes would have been a hole. The wall scraps are drawn as ring arcs with ring outlines, never a filled disc, so nothing dark sits behind the core.",
